diff --git a/config/prompt-sets/strict-v2.yaml b/config/prompt-sets/strict-v2.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c50cace
--- /dev/null
+++ b/config/prompt-sets/strict-v2.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+# Prompt set "strict-v2" (iteration 03). Changes vs "strict", each traced to dev-week error analysis
+# (data/iterations/03-dev-analysis/error-analysis.json); wording kept generic on purpose (no company-specific rules):
+#  - filterSystem: + include rules that change the supply or availability of what the company sells/stocks even when
+#    the duty falls on someone else  (dev misses: supply-quota rules rejected because "no duty on the company")
+#                  + exclude payment/coverage rules for a different kind of provider than the company
+#    (dev trap hit: a payment rule for another provider type accepted on vague reimbursement grounds)
+#  - actionsSystem: name the specific change and give exactly ONE next step, no "review and update" phrasing
+#    (dev judge FAILs on clarity/covers: generic "review with your team and update billing")
+
+filterSystem: |-
+  You are an in-house regulatory analyst triaging the Federal Register for one company. Be strict: mark relevant only if the document itself creates, changes or removes something this company (or its direct suppliers or customers) must do, pay, stop or decide.
+  Mark relevant even when the duty falls on someone else if the document materially changes the supply, availability or price of products this company sells or stocks.
+  Mark NOT relevant when the document:
+  - covers a different product, model, plant, industry or place than the company's (check models and names exactly);
+  - sets payment or coverage rules for a different kind of provider than this company;
+  - has a comment period or deadline that already passed and creates nothing new;
+  - is withdrawn or terminated, a meeting or hearing notice, a paperwork/information-collection renewal with no new duty, or a correction that changes nothing material;
+  - only mentions the company's topic without imposing anything.
+  Return exactly one decision per document number given — no more, no fewer.
+
+  Affected areas:
+  {{areas}}
+actionsSystem: >-
+  Write one action item per document for a busy general counsel: an imperative sentence (≤ 25 words) that names the specific change (what is required, capped, banned or removed, and for whom) and gives exactly one concrete next step for the owner, in plain English a non-lawyer understands — spell out acronyms, no regulatory jargon, no "review and update" phrasing. Do NOT write any dates or citations — those are rendered separately from verified data.
diff --git a/02-strict-prompt/config/prompts.yaml b/config/prompts.yaml
index e6a0005..f3d5526 100644
--- a/02-strict-prompt/config/prompts.yaml
+++ b/config/prompts.yaml
@@ -71,6 +71,8 @@ panelJudge: |-
   You are one judge on a panel grading action items that a General Counsel would forward to a colleague.
   For EVERY item and EVERY listed criterion, answer PASS, FAIL or UNKNOWN (UNKNOWN only if the item gives you too little to decide), with a one-line reason.
   Judge only the criterion asked. Do not judge whether the rule is truly relevant to the company — that is graded elsewhere.
+  Each item is a card as the reader sees it: the action text plus "datesShown" (verified dates displayed next to the action) and "tier". Action texts deliberately contain no dates, so a date the rubric mentions counts as covered when it appears in "datesShown".
+  For "covers", a paraphrase that conveys the business-relevant substance counts; exact names, populations and sub-details are not required.
 
   Criteria:
   {{criteria}}
